Package: InsectTrait
Type: Package
Title: Colour, Pattern and Shape Traits of Insects from Photographs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: Extracts colour, pattern and shape traits of insects from field
    photographs: single photos, folders of photos, folders sorted by species,
    or photos found through the Global Biodiversity Information Facility
    ('GBIF') and 'iNaturalist'. An optional 'Python' back end finds the insect
    with 'Grounding DINO' in two passes, outlines it with 'Segment Anything'
    2.1, screens each photo with a validated photo filter (usable photo, top or
    side view, butterfly wing side, several insects) and computes 67 traits.
    Core colour traits and outline quality metrics are also computed natively
    in R. Further functions apply validated decision rules, check colour casts
    and exposure, correct white balance, test trait stability under the
    rotations and colour changes used to augment training images, estimate
    photo-to-photo repeatability and invariance, and report a catalogue of
    trait reliability. The methods were developed and validated for insects
    only; they are not intended for birds or other animals.
